; The named lanes below are the same suite sliced by scenario family. They
; existed only as local commands, so every assertion in them was dead in CI:
; a PR could "fix" a lane scenario that nothing ever ran (found by the
; #32245 review). One rule per lane keeps a red lane's name in the failure
; output instead of one undifferentiated suite.

; Not on the runtest alias: the scenario passes end to end on macOS and the
; Linux runner stops later, widening back from a twelve-column pane, waiting
; for journal:full after Ctrl-N and Ctrl-F land on the narrow notice screen
; (run 34072434219). That step had never run anywhere either. The lane is
; named so it can be dispatched on its own while that is open.

; #37813 split the boot credential decision so a first install is told its
; workspace is not there yet instead of being handed a `masc login` command.
; The unit suite pins the sentence and the level; this lane pins what the
; operator sees -- the notice on the Overview events pane and no command.

; The per-PID stderr log held only the boot lines, so a session that ended left
; no reason behind -- roughly a hundred files a day and none said why. This lane
; quits the TUI and reads the reason back from the log the process wrote.

; RFC-0429 §4 asks a chat PTY scenario to show the mermaid drawing reaching
; the screen. test_tui_mermaid pins what the renderer produces; this pins that
; the fence is routed to it at all, which a golden cannot see.

; RFC-0429 §1.3/§4: the WHAT column projects a recorded newline to one cell.
; Its own lane because the default keyboard regression stops before the
; Changes surface, so an assertion added there would never run.

; #32469: the list row named the enqueue result and not what became of the
; wake, so a wake the queue cancelled forty seconds later read succeeded.
; Its own lane for the same reason as the one above -- the scenario sits
; behind the stall in the default keyboard regression (#34125).

; #32965: the writing footer offered q:quit while the draft took q as a
; letter. Its own lane because the Board draft is written behind the stall
; in the default keyboard regression (#34125).

; The spectator draws the machine's frame outside the frame presenter, and
; nothing walked that path. It is what holds the frame's shape: revert the grid
; to the window's own size and this lane reports 100 cells where the frame asks
; for 74.

(rule
 (alias runtest-test_tui_build_identity)
 (deps
  test_tui_build_identity.py
  ../bin/masc_tui.exe
  ../bin/main_eio.exe
  ../lib/build_commit/build_commit_generated.ml)
 (action
  (run python3 %{dep:test_tui_build_identity.py}
   %{dep:../bin/masc_tui.exe}
   %{dep:../lib/build_commit/build_commit_generated.ml}
   --server-binary %{dep:../bin/main_eio.exe}
   --expected-version %{version:masc})))

